<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Strabo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 64 BCE – c. 24 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Strabo was a Greek geographer and historian from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amasya">Amaseia</a> in Pontus, active under Augustus and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius">Tiberius</a>. His Geography, in seventeen books, describes the peoples, cities and lands of the Roman world from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. It is a principal source for many ancient peoples, towns and leagues that are otherwise poorly recorded.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/strabo.jpg" alt="Strabo" width="320" height="387" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: André Thévet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Strabo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
